    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n1. **Governance test failure**: The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `src/finetune/index.js`, but it was only available in the default export. Added explicit named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`.\n\n2. **Evaluation test failure**: The `toxicityMetric` function had an inconsistent signature. It expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` was calling it with `(outputs, references)` like the other metrics. This caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs as toxic. Changed the signature to accept `(outputs, references)` and always use the default banned terms.\n\nThe test suite now passes with all 28 tests green across 8 test files.",
